  "question": {
    "text": "If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>cos</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> has exactly <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math> solutions in the interval <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"⌉\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi>π</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>, then the roots of the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> belong to :",
    "image": null
  },
